.TH COMPRESS-JXL 1 "2026-07-01" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
compress-jxl \- batch compress images to JPEG XL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B compress-jxl.sh
[\fB\-q\fR \fIquality\fP]
[\fB\-e\fR \fIeffort\fP]
[\fB\-t\fR \fIthreads\fP]
[\fB\-c\fP]
[\fIdirectory\fP | \fIquality\fP [\fIeffort\fP]]
.br
.B compress-jxl.sh
[\fB\-h\fP | \fB\-\-help\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively finds all \fB.jpg\fP, \fB.jpeg\fP, and \fB.png\fP files under
the target directory and converts them to JPEG XL (\fB.jxl\fP) using
.BR cjxl (1).
Images larger than 2560\(mu1440 are downscaled before encoding.
The original file is replaced only if the compressed output is smaller.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quality " \fIquality\fP"
Quality target (0\(en100, default: 85).
Higher = larger file, better fidelity.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-effort " \fIeffort\fP"
Encoder effort (1\(en9, default: 4).
Higher = slower encode, smaller/better file.
.RS
.PD 0
.TP
1\(en2  lightning, decent compression
.TP
3\(en4  fast, good for batch runs
.TP
5\(en6  balanced
.TP
7     default cjxl speed, very good compression
.TP
8\(en9  exhaustive, noticeably slower
.PD
.RE
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-threads " \fIthreads\fP"
Parallel encode jobs (default: 4).
Each cjxl process auto-detects its own core count.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compare
Save a lossless PNG copy of each pre-encode source to
\fB/tmp/jxl_compare_src/\fP for later quality comparison
with tools like
.BR ssimulacra2 (1)
or
.BR dssim (1).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.PD 0
.TP
.I directory
Target directory (default: \fB~/Pictures/img\fP).
If relative, resolved under the default root.
.TP
.I quality
Numeric quality (0\(en100). If the first positional argument is a
number, it is treated as quality, not a directory.
.TP
.I effort
Numeric effort (1\(en9). Must follow a numeric quality.
.PD
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
compress-jxl.sh
Run with defaults: quality 85, effort 4, ~/Pictures/img.
.TP
compress-jxl.sh 80
Quality 80, effort 4, default directory.
.TP
compress-jxl.sh 90 7
Quality 90, effort 7, default directory.
.TP
compress-jxl.sh ~/Pictures/wallpapers 80 5
Custom directory, quality 80, effort 5.
.TP
compress-jxl.sh -q 75 -e 3 -t 6 -c ~/ai_art
Quality 75, effort 3, 6 parallel jobs, save comparison sources.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Pictures/img/.compress-jxl.log
Per-run summary appended after each successful batch.
.TP
.I /tmp/jxl_compare_src/
Directory holding pre-encode PNGs when \fB-c\fP is used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cjxl (1),
.BR ssimulacra2 (1)
